## Third-party dependencies

`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` holds the license text of every Go module linked into
the binary and of every package in the embedded graph UI. It ships in each
release `.zip` and as the release asset
`codegraph_<tag>_THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt`. `task licenses:notices` writes it.

Build-time and runtime dependencies are enumerated in `go.mod`, and a complete
SBOM (SPDX) is published as a release asset for every platform binary. To
inspect the exact dependency set compiled into a given release:

    gh release download <tag> -p 'codegraph_<tag>_<goos>_<goarch>.spdx.json'

Notable components:

- **tree-sitter** and its per-language grammars (MIT) — parsing. This is the
  project's main CGo dependency; the rationale is recorded in
  `PARSER-DECISION.md`.
- **fsnotify/fsevents** (BSD-3-Clause) — the macOS file watcher, through
  Apple's FSEvents API. It uses CGo and is linked only into macOS builds.
- **CockroachDB Pebble** (BSD-3-Clause) — the embedded graph store.
- **modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk** (Apache-2.0) — MCP server transport and tool registration.
- **spf13/cobra** (Apache-2.0) — CLI framework.

The binary also embeds the built graph UI from `web/build/`. Two components
of that bundle carry terms that go further than a copyright notice:

- **elkjs** 0.9.3 (EPL-2.0), the graph layout engine, used unmodified
  through cytoscape-elk. Its source code is available at
  <https://github.com/kieler/elkjs>, and the license text is at
  <https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/>.
- **Inter** (SIL Open Font License 1.1), the UI font, from the
  `@fontsource-variable/inter` package. Copyright 2016 The Inter Project
  Authors, <https://github.com/rsms/inter>. The license text is at
  <https://openfontlicense.org>.

The other UI packages are listed in `web/pnpm-lock.yaml`.

Each dependency retains its own license; nothing here supersedes them.
